# Classroom Prompt Builder (US MVP v1.1.2)

## Product

- **Site:** https://promptanatomy.online — free K–12 prompt builder + optional paid PDF guides ($4.99 / $9.99).
- **Stack:** static root (no build step) + Vercel serverless `api/*`.
- **Core files:** `index.html`, `success.html`, `privacy.html`, `terms.html`, `generator.js`, `copy.js`, `style.css`, `config/sot.json`.

## Repo boundary

- This repo is the **Vercel product + PDF fulfillment** repo: `promptanatomy.online`, Stripe checkout, Upstash Redis, Vercel Blob, transactional Resend, and `api/**`.
- School outreach is a separate sibling repo: `..\cpb-school-outreach` (Railway, Supabase Postgres, contact enrichment, campaign sending, marketing Resend on `news.promptanatomy.online`).
- Do **not** add outreach logic to Vercel `api/**`, Stripe fulfillment, Upstash, Blob, product env, or transactional email paths.
- For outreach tasks, work in `..\cpb-school-outreach` and follow its own `AGENTS.md` / Cursor rules.

## User-facing language

- All product copy is **en-US** (`lang="en-US"`). Teacher-friendly, concrete, concise.
- Do **not** use Lithuanian „Tu“ or informal LT tone in UI, legal, or email copy.

## Agent workflow

- Roles and stage-gate: [`AGENTS.md`](../../AGENTS.md).
- Internal agent docs may stay Lithuanian; **product** copy stays English.

## Documentation

- Active docs only via [`docs/INDEX.md`](../../docs/INDEX.md).
- Operator scratch (not INDEX, not archived): [`todo.md`](../../todo.md), [`memo_pdf.md`](../../memo_pdf.md).

## Single source of truth (SOT)

- [`config/sot.json`](../../config/sot.json) — modes, theme, `commerce`, `pdfGuides`, `buyerFaq`, `legal`.
- Commerce copy and Stripe URLs: `config/sot.json#commerce` — hydrate via `data-commerce-*` / `data-stripe-cta` hooks in `index.html`, not hardcoded marketing strings.

## Security

- Never commit secrets (`.env`, API keys, tokens).
- Production API: no sensitive data in logs; avoid `console.log` in shipped paths.

## Quality gates (summary)

| Change | Run |
|--------|-----|
| Any code/docs | `npm test` |
| UX / HTML interactions | `npm run test:smoke`, `npm run test:a11y` |
| Forms, sessions, copy, modes | `npm run test:e2e` (core-flow) |
| PDF commerce CSS / layout | `npm run test:e2e` (includes mobile-pdf-commerce) |
| Fulfillment `api/**` | `npm test`; recommend `npm run check:fulfillment` before deploy |

**CI truth:** `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs `npm run test:mixed` — match or exceed locally before PR.

## Specialized rules

- PDF commerce UI: `.cursor/rules/cpb-pdf-commerce.mdc`
- Stripe fulfillment: `.cursor/rules/cpb-fulfillment.mdc`
